Using the quadrature rules of Section~\ref{ssec:quadForIRF}, we discretize the continuous norm in~\eqref{eq:minProbIRF} and write the minimization problem as,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:minProb}
    \min_{\mathbf{a}, \mathbf{b}} \, \sum_{k=1}^K \sum_{n=0}^N{ \dfrac{\sqrt{\lambda_k}}{\widehat{Q}(z_k)}\left|{b_n z_k^n - a_n z_k^n \widehat{W}(z_k) }\right|}
\end{equation}
in which the unknowns are the monomial coefficients of $P(z)$ and $Q(z)$, denoted $\mathbf{b}$ and $\mathbf{a}$, respectively.
